  "result": "`slugify(text)` is now implemented in `src/strings.js`, and `npm test` passes all 13 tests (2 existing, 11 new).\n\nIt does the following, in order:\n- `đ` and `Đ` become `d`.\n- The text is decomposed so combining accents can be stripped, which leaves plain ASCII for Vietnamese and other Latin text.\n- The text is lowercased.\n- Every run of characters outside `a-z` and `0-9` becomes a single hyphen.\n- Leading hyphens are removed, the result is cut to 50 characters, and any trailing hyphens are removed after the cut. This ordering is what stops a slug cut at 50 from ending in a hyphen.\n\nThe new tests in `test/strings.test.js` cover:\n- lowercasing and hyphenation\n- Vietnamese and other Latin diacritics\n- `đ`/`Đ`\n- runs of punctuation\n- hyphen trimming\n- digits\n- empty and symbol-only input\n- the 50-character cut, including a cut that lands on a hyphen and a 50-character slug that ends on a letter\n\nMy first draft of two of the length tests miscounted characters and failed. The bug was in the tests, not in `slugify`, and I corrected them.",
